.Dd 2026-11-08
.Dt LBTS-SEARCH 1
.\" Manual page created by:
.\" Guus Sliepen <guus@lightbts.info>
.Sh NAME
.Nm lbts search
.Nd search the text of all messages
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm lbts search
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl -sort Ar field
.Op Fl -json
.Ar word ...
.Op Fl - Ar selector ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The command lists the tickets with messages whose subject or text contains all the given words,
best match first, in the same format as
.Nm lbts list .
Pseudo-headers are not searched.
.Pp
Words are matched as whole words, ignoring case.
The query uses the syntax of the full-text search of SQLite:
.Ql OR
and
.Ql NOT
combine words, a word ending in
.Ql *
matches every word that starts with it, and words between double quotes must appear as a phrase.
Words with other characters, like
.Ql lbts-web ,
are searched for as a phrase.
.Pp
Selectors after
.Ql --
limit which tickets are searched, see
.Xr lbts-fields 5 .
Like
.Nm lbts list ,
only open tickets are searched by default.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Show a part of each matching message, with the matching words between
.Ql \&[
and
.Ql \&] .
.It Fl -sort Ar field
Sort the tickets by a field instead of by how well they match.
.It Fl -json
Write the tickets as with
.Ql lbts list --json ,
with an additional array
.Va matches
of objects with the
.Va message_id
and
.Va snippet
of each matching message.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
lbts search index
lbts search '"wrong index"' OR crlf -- all
lbts search -v reind* -- closed tags=patch
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lbts 1 ,
.Xr lbts-fields 5 .
.Sh AUTHOR
.An "Guus Sliepen" Aq guus@lightbts.info
